{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CartanContraction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CartanContraction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.d_iota_eq_zero_of_closed_of_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.d_iota_eq_zero_of_closed_of_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/CartanContraction.lean#L56-L66","doc":"**Cartan contraction step.** If `ω` is closed (`d ω = 0`) and\nflow-invariant (`lie ω = 0`), its contraction `iota ω` is closed.\nGeometric reading: a Reeb-invariant closed 4-form contracts to a\nclosed 3-form, whose de Rham class is an invariant of the flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.lie_apply_eq_d_iota_of_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.lie_apply_eq_d_iota_of_closed","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/CartanContraction.lean#L45-L54","doc":"On a closed element (`d ω = 0`), Cartan's homotopy formula collapses\nto `lie ω = d (iota ω)`: the Lie derivative of a closed form is exact,\nwith primitive its contraction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}